// Phase 1: Backend infrastructure & seed data (independently parallelizable)
await runs.run('backend', {
  agent: 'qwen',
  task: `Create the complete Node.js backend for a spreadsheet app at /workspace/template/.factory26/20260928-025750-fb85c109/braid-state/worktrees/issue-3/pi-qwen-fast-g1/backend/.

Tech stack: Node.js 20+, Express, JSON file storage (no database). Use environment variable DATA_DIR for storage location, defaulting to ./data/. Start with PORT env var (default 3000), HOST=0.0.0.0. Serve built frontend static files from dist/.

1. Create package.json with express dependency. Run npm install.

2. Seed data (created on first startup if data dir doesn't exist):
   Workbooks array stored as backend/data/workbooks.json:
   {
     "id": "seed-workbook",
     "name": "Q3 Sales",
     "createdAt": "<ISO timestamp>",
     "lastUpdated": "<ISO timestamp of creation>",
     "sheets": [
       {
         "id": "sheet1-id",
         "name": "Sheet1",
         "cells": {
           "A1": { "v": "Region" },
           "A2": { "v": "East" },
           "B2": { "v": "1200" },
           "A3": { "v": "North" },
           "B3": { "v": "800" }
         },
         "selection": { "range": "A1" },
         "rowHeights": {},
         "colWidths": {}
       },
       {
         "id": "sheet2-id",
         "name": "Sheet2",
         "cells": {
           "A1": { "v": "Region" },
           "A2": { "v": "East" },
           "B2": { "v": "1200" },
           "A3": { "v": "North" },
           "B3": { "v": "800" }
         },
         "selection": { "range": "A1" },
         "rowHeights": {},
         "colWidths": {}
       }
     ],
     "activeSheetId": "sheet1-id",
     "lastSaved": "<ISO timestamp>"
   }

3. REST API endpoints (all return JSON):
   - GET    /api/workbooks          - List all workbooks (return array of {id,name,lastUpdated})
   - POST   /api/workbooks          - Create new blank workbook -> {id, name:"New Workbook", sheets:[{id,newName:"Sheet1", cells:{}, selection:{range:"A1"}}], activeSheetId}
   - GET    /api/workbooks/:id      - Get full workbook state (ALL fields above)
   - PATCH  /api/workbooks/:id      - Update workbook name: {name: "new name"} -> updates lastUpdated
   - DELETE /api/workbooks/:id      - Delete workbook
   - GET    /api/workbooks/:id/sheets - Get sheet list [{id,name}]
   - PUT    /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/order - Reorder: {order:["id1","id2"]} -> update order, lastUpdated
   - POST   /api/workbooks/:id/sheets - Create new sheet: returns updated workbook with new sheet
   - PATCH  /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId - Update sheet fields ({name?, cells?, selection?, rowHeights?, colWidths?}) -> updates lastUpdated
   - DELETE /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId - Delete sheet (must leave >=1 sheet)
   - PUT    /api/workbooks/:id/active-sheet - Set active sheet: {sheetId} -> lastUpdated

4. All modification endpoints must update lastUpdated timestamp after success.

5. Server entry: server.js — listens on PORT, serves static dist/ for non-API routes.

Write all code in one go: package.json, server.js, seed data logic, and ensure it starts cleanly. Do NOT run npm install inside the agent; just create files.`
})

